<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Intuition stage, the cognition's decision layer (the later tier
  that answers in words is the hand_ons tier intuition, decisions D140 and
  D144): the fast System 1 pick, made by the decision service (never by a
  free-text model) over the turn's choices, with a self-tuning confidence
  gate. The cognition (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx) invokes it once
  per turn after autonomy left the turn unhandled.

    deciding (an invoked decision service) -> done

  Processor (the decision service's kind predicate): the turn's choices,
  the <param> choices (the
  body's assembled snapshot choices: its own enabled event:schema
  transitions and what each ability offers that turn, tagged with the offering
  ability as target), within the decision layer's effort ceiling (the
  cognition frames them, decision D206), go to the
  decision service, which never offers the deliberate handoff
  bot.ability.reasoning.input. Its state is {turn: T}, T the model-facing
  text of the stimulus (<cognition:model_facing_content>, decision
  D150: what reasoning reads, never the raw envelope), after the <held>
  block of the actions over the ceiling (the <param> held, decision
  D206), which the decision cannot choose and only a pass hands on; the
  stimulus goes too, but only to ground each event's required data from its
  data's value, else the schema's enum; an event it cannot fill is not
  offered, so a reply that needs free text goes on to a later tier (user
  answer, 2026-10-08). The service adds one pass criterion per tier of
  hand_ons (the <param>; reasoning alone until the cognition composes a
  chat tier, decision D150). When a pass wins (declined) or nothing could be filled
  (no-candidates) the product is empty: the turn escalates with the
  reason empty_product, a pass naming its tier as hand_to, and
  the tuner observes nothing. Otherwise the service returns only the chosen
  event, with its data and its probability as its confidence
  (decision.selected, decision D150).

  Context fit (decision D150): with a
  max_context_tokens <param>, the service cuts the decision's instructions
  to fit floor(max_context_tokens * bytes_per_token) bytes of request; its
  done data reports the request's bytes and the tokens the backend counted,
  and the stage keeps the fewest bytes a token any answer showed in
  bytes_per_token (a <param>, 3 to start), which goes back in <donedata> for
  the cognition to keep across turns.

  Confidence (0-100 scale): the tuner state
  {mean, var, n}, the confidence_tuner datum, comes in as a <param> and
  goes back in <donedata>, so it lives in the cognition across turns. The
  turn's confidence is its selection's probability normalized to a whole
  0-100 number (<processing:selection_confidence>). <intuition:observe>
  observes it first (a null confidence is not observed), then
  <intuition:escalate> writes whether it is below the updated threshold
  (the defaults: the floor 35 during the warmup of 8
  observations, then max(floor / 2, mean - k_sigma * std); EMA alpha 0.08,
  variance floor 100), and the turn escalates when it is (observe, then
  escalate).

  Classification: a confident product is handled, its selection {event, data,
  target} (escalation reason none). A low-confidence product
  (low_confidence), or one holding bot.ability.reasoning.input
  (deliberative_input), is unhandled and escalates. The decision timer is
  deciding.after (decision_timeout_ms, a <param> the cognition sets from
  its bounds).

  Dispatch (decision D113): the stage sends, before it
  answers, what it acted on to its target, the session that offers it (the
  decision service names a selection's only offerer): a handled product's selection, the ignore included
  (it goes to the cognition, which only logs it), and of an escalating
  product only the environment actions, never the ignore or the deliberate
  handoff, sent before the next tier runs. What it sent is acted in every
  <donedata> ([] when nothing), so the cognition knows it as a fact of the
  turn. The decision service has checked the
  selection's data against its event's schema (the pinned focus device
  among them), so nothing is refused at the send, and there is no re-ask
  with a rejection as feedback.

  Output: <donedata>, received by the cognition as done.invoke.intuition:

    {turn, handled: true, selected: [{event, data, target}], acted, reason: "none", confidence_tuner, bytes_per_token}
    {turn, handled: false, reason, hand_to?, acted, confidence_tuner, bytes_per_token}  (escalate)
    {turn, handled: false, failed: true, reason, acted, confidence_tuner, bytes_per_token}

  The stage answers once the service has ended (done.invoke.decision, whose
  data teaches bytes_per_token) after its one event. A decision.failed,
  error.*, or no answer within decision_timeout_ms fails the stage (the
  cognition answers the turn with bot.ability.failed); the cognition's hop
  timeout bounds the whole stage too.

  Bindings: the intuition, processing and cognition namespace packages and
  the decision service package, resolved from their repository URIs; env
  scopes TYPESAFE_API_KEY and TYPESAFE_BASE_URL to the service's <invoke>
  (without either it answers decision.failed unconfigured; a base URL
  without a key is asked keyless). An invoked service's events are not
  checked against event:schema (scxml.rs checks only events between SCXML
  sessions): the decision service validates the selection's data against
  the choices' schema for it before returning it, and its own events are
  shape-checked by cond (Object(...) reads a non-object as {}).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:cognition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/cognition"
       xmlns:intuition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/intuition"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="intuition" initial="deciding">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The turn, from the cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The actions held from this tier, over its effort ceiling (decision
         D206): {event, description?} each, rendered as the <held> block of
         the state the decision reads, so a pass can hand them on. -->
    <data id="held" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The bot's environment (decision D106): the decision's situation once
         the cognition's situation renderer gives it one (D150). -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <data id="confidence_tuner" expr="({mean: 70, var: 100, n: 0})"/>
    <data id="decision_timeout_ms" expr="20000"/>
    <!-- The later tiers a pass may hand the turn to (decision D150). -->
    <data id="hand_ons" expr="['reasoning']"/>
    <!-- The decision model's context fit (null sends every request
         whole) and the bytes a token learned so far. -->
    <data id="max_context_tokens" expr="null"/>
    <data id="bytes_per_token" expr="3"/>
    <!-- The decision in flight: the stimulus's model-facing text. -->
    <data id="stimulus_content" expr="null"/>
    <data id="confidence" expr="null"/>
    <data id="escalate" expr="false"/>
    <data id="decision_timer" expr="null"/>
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <data id="failed_code" expr="null"/>
    <!-- What the stage sent, and the selection being sent (the <foreach>
         item). -->
    <data id="acted" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="intuition.js"/>

  <state id="deciding">
    <onentry>
      <send idlocation="decision_timer" event="deciding.after" delayexpr="decisionTimeoutDelay()"/>
      <cognition:model_facing_content location="stimulus_content" stimulus="stimulus"
                                      prior_episodes="[]" standing_directives="[]" held="held"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendidexpr="decision_timer"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke id="decision" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/decision"
            env:apikey="TYPESAFE_API_KEY" env:baseurl="TYPESAFE_BASE_URL">
      <param name="kind" expr="'predicate'"/>
      <param name="choices" expr="choices"/>
      <param name="state" expr="decisionState()"/>
      <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
      <param name="hand_ons" expr="hand_ons"/>
      <param name="max_context_tokens" expr="max_context_tokens"/>
      <param name="bytes_per_token" expr="bytes_per_token"/>
    </invoke>

    <!-- The decision service's own events: the stage answers once the
         service has ended. The chosen event, with its confidence: observe
         it, then escalate when it is below the updated threshold. -->
    <transition event="decision.selected" cond="hasSelections(_event)">
      <processing:selection_confidence location="confidence" selections="_event.data.selections"/>
      <intuition:observe location="confidence_tuner" confidence="confidence"/>
      <intuition:escalate location="escalate" confidence="confidence" tuner="confidence_tuner"/>
      <log label="intuition" expr="tunedLog(_event)"/>
      <if cond="escalate">
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('low_confidence')"/>
      <elseif cond="hasDeliberativeInput(_event)"/>
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('deliberative_input')"/>
      <else/>
        <assign location="result" expr="selectionResult(_event)"/>
      </if>
      <assign location="acted" expr="actedSelections(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result.acted" expr="acted"/>
      <foreach array="acted" item="s">
        <send eventexpr="s.event" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + s.target">
          <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.abstain" cond="isAbstainReason(_event)">
      <log label="intuition" expr="abstainedLog(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="abstainedResult(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.failed">
      <assign location="failed_code" expr="failedCode(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="decisionFailedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The service's done data: the request's bytes and the tokens the
         backend counted teach the bytes a token. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke.decision" cond="hasResult()" target="done">
      <assign location="bytes_per_token" expr="learnedBytesPerToken(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result.bytes_per_token" expr="bytes_per_token"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The service ended without an answer: the timer decides. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke.decision"/>
    <transition event="deciding.after" cond="hasResult()" target="done"/>
    <transition event="deciding.after" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="timedOutResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Once the decision has answered, an error is not the decision's. -->
    <transition event="error.*" cond="hasResult()"/>
    <transition event="error.*" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="couldNotRunResult(_event)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <final id="done">
    <donedata>
      <content expr="result"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
